# CSS class naming (camelCase)

Use **camelCase** for every class name. Do not use kebab-case, underscores, or strict BEM separators (`__`, `--`) in class strings.

## Pattern

- **Single-word block**: lowercase — `home`, `card`, `modal` — when the block name is one word.
- **Multi-word block**: camelCase — `siteHeader`, `productCard`.
- **Block + element**: concatenate with a capital — e.g. block `home` → `homeHeader`, `homeTitle`, `homeHero`.
- **Modifier**: prefer a second camelCase class — e.g. `btn btnPrimary`, `card cardHighlighted`. Or one compound class — e.g. `cardExpanded`, `menuOpen`.
Keep names short; avoid deeply stacked compounds (`fooBarBazQuux`) unless necessary.

## Examples

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.home { }
.homeHeader { }
.homeTitle { }
.homeHero { }
.siteHeader { }

/* ❌ BAD */
.home-header { }
.home__title { }
.card__body--compact { }
```

Use the **same** class strings in React `className`. Class names are case-sensitive in HTML/CSS, so typos in casing break styles.
